 abstract={Copper and zinc were incorporated into plasma electrolytic oxidation (PEO) coatings on grade-2 titanium using an alternating-current process in which only the electrical waveform was varied, yielding two doping levels. The coated surfaces were evaluated for surface properties, human gingival fibroblast and osteoblast responses, and antibacterial effects against Staphylococcus aureus and Aggregatibacter actinomycetemcomitans.},
